<title>GERMANY: Kloeckner-Werke breaks even in 1995/96.</title>
<headline>Kloeckner-Werke breaks even in 1995/96.</headline>
<dateline>DUISBURG, Germany 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kloeckner-Werke AG, the German engineering group, said on Wednesday that it broke even as expected in the business year that ended on September 30 after a loss of 210 million marks the year before.</p>
<p>&quot;All business divisions improved considerably from the previous year,&quot; the company said in a regulatory statement.</p>
<p>The company said sales rose three percent to 4.5 billion marks in 1995/96. The workforce declined five percent to 18,242 employees.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
